<p>A further point of practice emerges from the way the case was fought. The husband's failure to cross-examine the wife effectively did substantial damage to his position, since her testimony on the family's circumstances went largely unchallenged. In maintenance proceedings, where the paying spouse's true income is rarely capable of documentary proof, the cross-examination is often where the case is decided.</p>
